1
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:24,220
planet, hurtling through space, covered by more than 70% water,

2
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:28,140
our ocean is bursting with life.

3
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:31,980
And it gives life, producing half the oxygen we breathe

4
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:35,460
and critical food for half the world's population.

5
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:38,580
It connects us, serving as a super highway

6
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,620
for international trade.

7
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:44,780
And it inspires us, providing open space for recreation

8
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:47,460
and exploration.

9
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:50,020
For more than 50 years, NOAA has been

10
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:53,940
at the forefront of conserving, managing, and exploring

11
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:57,060
this vast resource to benefit Americans now

12
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:59,660
and for generations to come.

13
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:03,980
This is the idea behind a sustainable and resilient

14
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,030
American blue economy.

15
00:01:10,030 --> 00:01:13,910
At NOAA, we continue to unravel new mysteries

16
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:18,470
from the ocean's surface to its deepest depths.

17
00:01:18,470 --> 00:01:20,510
Our ships and those of our partners

18
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:24,510
are mapping and exploring the largely unknown ocean,

19
00:01:24,510 --> 00:01:26,750
expanding our knowledge and discovering

20
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:30,110
new medicines, food, and energy sources.

21
00:01:30,110 --> 00:01:33,750
After all, we can't realize the ocean's full potential

22
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:36,190
without knowing what's out there.

23
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:40,510
As our reach into the ocean expands, what will we discover?

24
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:50,930
What will demand our protection or inspire future explorers?

25
00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:53,970
NOAA is already protecting natural wonders

26
00:01:53,970 --> 00:01:56,250
from coast to coast through our national marine

27
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:59,450
sanctuaries and marine national monuments.

28
00:01:59,450 --> 00:02:02,370
Like our national parks, national marine sanctuaries

29
00:02:02,370 --> 00:02:04,410
are open to all.

30
00:02:04,410 --> 00:02:07,930
Whether exploring a shipwreck, diving around towering

31
00:02:07,930 --> 00:02:10,050
kelp forests, or whale watching,

32
00:02:10,050 --> 00:02:13,250
we've got something for everyone to enjoy.

33
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:16,250
More than sites of conservation and recreation,

34
00:02:16,250 --> 00:02:19,730
marine sanctuaries generate billions of dollars a year

35
00:02:19,730 --> 00:02:21,410
for local communities.

36
00:02:21,410 --> 00:02:25,130
Tourism and recreation account for the largest sector

37
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:30,370
of the blue economy.

38
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:33,050
NOAA Fisheries Management, in cooperation

39
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:35,930
with state, regional, and tribal partners,

40
00:02:35,930 --> 00:02:38,730
is the gold standard for resource protection.

41
00:02:38,730 --> 00:02:42,170
As a result, the US has emerged as a global leader

42
00:02:42,170 --> 00:02:44,330
in sustainable seafood.

43
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:47,690
Wild caught and farmed seafood generate billions of dollars

44
00:02:47,690 --> 00:02:51,250
annually, employing millions of Americans.

45
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:55,570
As seafood demand grows, so will economic opportunities.

46
00:02:55,570 --> 00:02:58,810
NOAA is working with fishermen and ocean farmers

47
00:02:58,810 --> 00:03:01,450
to drive innovation and job growth.

48
00:03:01,450 --> 00:03:04,730
We're committed to securing a sustainable future

49
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:11,070
for this indispensable food source.

50
00:03:11,070 --> 00:03:13,310
NOAA is helping coastal communities

51
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:15,790
weather a changing climate.

52
00:03:15,790 --> 00:03:19,230
We generate sea level rise forecasts and critical storm

53
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:22,550
data to empower communities to plan and build

54
00:03:22,550 --> 00:03:24,510
a resilient future.

55
00:03:24,510 --> 00:03:27,310
We look to the natural world, supporting projects

56
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:30,550
that enhance natural barriers, like oyster and coral reefs,

57
00:03:30,550 --> 00:03:32,430
which protect our coasts.

58
00:03:32,430 --> 00:03:35,790
This blend of high and low tech preparedness

59
00:03:35,790 --> 00:03:44,260
fortifies communities to bounce back after a storm.

60
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:47,620
At NOAA, we're bridging the vast expanse of the ocean,

61
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:50,860
connecting the US with the global economy.

62
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,740
To meet increased demand for goods,

63
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:56,340
NOAA's flagship weather forecast and navigation programs

64
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:59,220
guide enormous ships, safeguarding trillions

65
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:02,420
of dollars in economic activity.

66
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:04,740
We also work to survey waterways

67
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:08,380
and protect sensitive habitats when storms or accidents

68
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:12,060
occur, ensuring the international superhighway

69
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:16,240
stays open.

70
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:18,920
For more than 50 years, NOAA has

71
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:22,160
been leading in the understanding and sustainable use

72
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:25,800
of our ocean, making amazing discoveries,

73
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:30,000
protecting ocean wonders, enhancing sustainable seafood

74
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,880
output, preparing us for climate change,

75
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:35,880
and supporting ocean-based trade.

76
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:39,760
Our global blue economy is as diverse, interconnected,

77
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:42,840
and resilient as our blue planet,

78
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:48,200
and is forecast to accelerate, doubling by 2030.

79
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:51,000
Building on 50 years of experience,

80
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,040
NOAA will continue to lead the way.

